# 14. Controllers and Routes Roadmap

After all database foundations are ready, Codex must implement controllers one module at a time.

Suggested route groups:

```text
/dashboard

/accounts
/account-types

/category-groups
/categories

/payees

/transactions
/transfers
/recurring-transactions

/budgets

/credit-cards
/credit-card-invoices
/credit-card-purchases

/shopping-lists
/purchases

/settings
```

Each module should include:

```text
index
create
store
show
edit
update
destroy/archive
restore
```

Important:

The destroy action should usually archive the record instead of deleting it.

---

# 15. UI Pages Roadmap

Each page should follow the project frontend conventions (Inertia + Vue).

## 15.1 Dashboard

The dashboard should show:

- Total balance
- Account balances
- Monthly income
- Monthly expenses
- Current month result
- Pending transactions
- Upcoming recurring transactions
- Open credit card invoices
- Budget alerts

## 15.2 Accounts page

Should include:

- Account list
- Account type
- Current balance
- Archived status
- Create/edit form

## 15.3 Transactions page

Should include:

- Filters by period
- Filters by account
- Filters by category
- Filters by type
- Filters by status
- Transaction table
- Create transaction button

## 15.4 Credit cards page

Should include:

- Card list
- Limit
- Current invoice
- Due date
- Invoice status

## 15.5 Budgets page

Should include:

- Budget list
- Used amount
- Remaining amount
- Usage percentage
- Alert indicator

## 15.6 Shopping lists page

Should include:

- List of shopping lists
- Items
- Estimated total
- Checked/unchecked items using Vue state

---

# 16. Validation Strategy

Use AdonisJS validators or request validation classes.

Every form must validate:

- Required fields
- Numeric values
- Dates
- Enum values
- Ownership of related records

Important ownership rule:

A user must never be able to link records belonging to another user.

Example:

A transaction cannot be created using another user’s account.

---

# 17. Authorization and Authentication

Authentication base is already implemented and must be refined after the base database structure.

Required features:

- Register
- Login
- Logout
- Protected routes
- Current authenticated user scope

All user-owned queries must be scoped by:

```text
user_id
```

Example:

```ts
.where('user_id', auth.user.id)
```

---

# 18. Business Logic Services

Codex should avoid placing all business logic inside controllers.

Create services when needed.

Suggested services:

```text
app/services/transaction_service.ts
app/services/transfer_service.ts
app/services/recurring_transaction_service.ts
app/services/budget_service.ts
app/services/credit_card_invoice_service.ts
app/services/credit_card_payment_service.ts
app/services/shopping_purchase_service.ts
```

## 18.1 TransactionService

Responsibilities:

- Create income transaction
- Create expense transaction
- Update account balance
- Cancel transaction
- Archive transaction
- Recalculate account balance if needed

## 18.2 TransferService

Responsibilities:

- Create transfer
- Create source transaction
- Create destination transaction
- Validate source and destination accounts
- Keep transfer atomic using database transaction

## 18.3 CreditCardInvoiceService

Responsibilities:

- Create or find invoice by card and date
- Attach purchases to invoices
- Close invoice
- Calculate invoice total
- Mark invoice as paid or partially paid

## 18.4 CreditCardPaymentService

Responsibilities:

- Pay invoice
- Create invoice payment record
- Create account transaction
- Update invoice paid amount
- Update invoice status

## 18.5 BudgetService

Responsibilities:

- Calculate budget usage
- Calculate remaining amount
- Detect warning threshold
- Filter transactions by budget period and categories

---

# 19. Atomic Operations

The following operations must use database transactions:

```text
Creating a transfer
Paying a credit card invoice
Creating an installment purchase
Closing an invoice
Creating a purchase with purchase items and transaction
Deleting or archiving records that affect balances
```

Reason:

These operations affect multiple tables and must not leave the database inconsistent.

---

# 20. MVP Scope

The first usable MVP should include:

```text
Authentication
Settings
Accounts
Categories
Payees
Transactions
Transfers
Basic dashboard
Basic recurring transactions CRUD
Basic budgets CRUD
Basic credit card CRUD
Basic credit card invoice listing
Shopping lists CRUD
```

The MVP does not need:

```text
Automatic bank integration
Pix integration
Open Finance
Multi-currency
Mobile app
PDF reports
Complex charts
Background jobs
Advanced permissions
Family sharing
AI features
```

---

